{
  "id": "xplane12-b738-fms",
  "aircraft": "Boeing 737-800",
  "label": "X-Plane 12 default 737-800 FMS/CDU",
  "description": "Screen and keypad mapping for X-Plane 12's built-in default FMS, confirmed live against a running X-Plane 12.4.3 with the stock Boeing 737-800 (ICAO B738) loaded (2026-08-10). Same generic sim/FMS / sim/FMS2 / sim/CDU3 command set and screen datarefs as default-fms.json (the default FMS/CDU program is shared across Laminar's own default aircraft, not implemented per-airframe) — confirmed by firing sim/FMS/index and sim/FMS/fpln live and reading back the resulting CDU page titles (INDEX page was already showing; fpln brought up the ACT FPLN/ROUTE page, matching the 737's real 'RTE' key). Only the physical bezel layout and a couple of button labels differ from the Airbus profile; see keypadLayout below and each key's optional 'label' override. This is NOT the same as Zibo's 737 addon, which replaces the default systems/avionics wholesale with its own custom implementation under an entirely different namespace — this profile only applies to the bare Laminar-default 737-800.",

  "screen": {
    "lines": 14,
    "cols": 24,
    "textDatarefTemplate": "sim/cockpit2/radios/indicators/fms_cdu{cdu}_text_line{line}",
    "styleDatarefTemplate": "sim/cockpit2/radios/indicators/fms_cdu{cdu}_style_line{line}"
  },

  "commandPrefixByCdu": {
    "1": "sim/FMS",
    "2": "sim/FMS2",
    "3": "sim/CDU3"
  },

  "_note_on_brightness": "No CDU brightness command/dataref found for the 737 yet — the real hardware has a rotary BRT knob here (not up/down buttons like the Airbus's laminar/A333/buttons/fmsN_brightness_up/dn), and nothing under sim/FMS*, laminar/B738/*, or the generic sim/cockpit2/*/instrument_brightness_ratio* datarefs obviously matched it in a live scan. Left unwired rather than guessed — see ARCHITECTURE.md's roadmap.",

